Sequence is a rythm game with an actual story (not a bad one in my opinion), but won't spoil it :P it has combat mechanics which really few games have done it well if any. you have 3 "panels/tabs" in which you run the rythms, the atack one, defese one and mana gathering one, it's basics are well explained in it's well made tutorial.
Cons:
- if you want to 100% can be a tinsy but grindy to get materials for crafting ( YES IT HAS CRAFTING);
- for a rythm game it doesn't have that many songs;
Pros:
- an actual decent story with twist;
- good, funny dialogue with great voice acting;
- challenging yet fun gameplay;
- nice variety of skills;
- has crafting and items with boosts and what not's;
- cartoony/anime graphics but well made in my opinion;
- trains observatory and reflex skills;
- story wise doesn't have replayability but it's fun to replay it from time to time;
- story easter egg, FIND IT;
- not hard to 100%;
- you can pause during battles whenever you want;

I published a first review about this game a few hours ago. Maybe it wasn't clear for some people previously, so I'll try again to make them understand better about my opinion on this game:
As a Worms Ultimate Mayhem player, I was curious about this WWPR and I purchased it to find out if it's a good Worms. The thing is, I couldn't have gone far enough. Why? Probably not because of the game itself, which seems quite feature-rich and fun for some players here. I requested (and obtained) a refund because of the so-called remastering we've been promised. I think it is just some kind of emulation of the old game, with some tweaks to ensure it works on the latest Windows:
1-Menus and UI (in Menus) aren't upscaled, they are stuck to default resolution from back then when the game was released for the first time;
2-There's no Windowed mode (I guess it wasn't available in the first release either, but for a remaster, we could have expected to see such a "basic" feature available on day one);
3-Alt+Tab should be avoided with this game (I was stuck once, unable to do anything with the mouse, I had to open the task manager and kill the game, hurray...);
4-The 1080p/60 fps combo: 1080p only during a match, and framerate usually drops to 50 and below.
Selling a game with such a price for such a lazy emulation is quite steep...
You'd better keep playing at your current Worms titles than buying this one.

