First of all, the graphics are absolutely gorgeous and stunning, some of the best visuals I've seen in games. Additionally to that, the soundtrack is amazing and fits perfectly to the mood of the game. Put those together and you get an incredibly immersive game that really sucks you in. And that already makes for 60% of the experience - wandering around in that beautiful world and enjoying the atmosphere is just perfect. You really have to play the game slowly to get the most out of it. (loud headphones and a dark room are helpful, too)
But on to the actual game part. You play as a private detective, who has the ability to communicate with the dead to some degree. He comes to Red Creek Valley after the young boy Ethan Carter sends him a letter asking for help. The purpose of the game is to find out what happened in Red Creek Valley - a place with dark secrets, as you find out quickly. This is done by exploring the area (
), finding out the background to murders and solving (mostly easy) riddles. During all that the game does not give you any objectives, there isn't even a real HUD - "This game is a narrative experience that does not hold your hand" is a statement that pops up in the beginning of the game, and it is 100% accurate. Playtime is around 5 hours, which is a bit short, but then again the game is no full price title. Still the price could be a bit cheaper.

